{"/api/discogs/artist/14661/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"14661","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Adnb3byx9E4yH1BSzwvOE-hu42aMGxtBKXL7wDZggHs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:498/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE0NjYx/LTE1MTA5MzM1MTAt/NDczOS5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/cscr9WkKxuFB2YivmaJ9l5OiJuvyWGZOVEcSGJf_nQg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE0NjYx/LTE1MTA5MzM1MTAt/NDczOS5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"South African flugelhorn, trumpet and cornet player (4 April 1939 - 23 January 2018). In 1961, as part of the anti-apartheid campaign, he was exiled to the United States where he was befriended by [a=Harry Belafonte]. Primarily, he played in jazz ensembles, with guest appearances on albums by [a=The Byrds], and [a=Paul Simon]. Masekela was a former collaborator of [a=Abdullah Ibrahim]. He is reported to have been initially inspired in his musical growth by Trevor Huddleston, a British priest working in the South African townships who financed Masekela's first trumpet. Masekela played his way through the Sophiatown scene with [a=The Jazz Epistles] and to Britain with King Kong, to find himself in New York in the early-1960s. He had hits in the United States with the pop-jazz tunes Up, Up And Away and the number one hit Grazing In The Grass. In 1987, his single Bring Him Back Home became an anthem for the movement to free Nelson Mandela. After apartheid ended, Masekela returned to South Africa. A renewed interest in his African roots led him to collaborate with West and Central African musicians, and finally to reconnect with South African players when he set up a mobile studio in Botswana, just over the South African border, in the 1980s. Here he re-absorbed and re-used mbaqanga strains, a style he has continued to use since his return to South Africa in the early-1990s.\r\n\r\n[b]Born:[/b] 4th April 1939, in Witbank, Mpumalanga, South Africa.\r\n[b]Died:[/b] 23rd January 2018, in Johannesburg, Gauteng, South Africa [from prostate cancer, aged 78].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:14661","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":305163,"name":"Philemon Hou"},{"id":937223,"name":"The Disco Kid"},{"id":7212806,"name":"Ramapolo"}],"groups":[{"active":true,"id":268036,"name":"Hugh Masekela & The Union Of South Africa"},{"active":true,"id":1574785,"name":"The Jazz Epistles"},{"active":true,"id":4136007,"name":"Masekela And His African Beat Band"},{"active":true,"id":7674954,"name":"Hugh Masekela Quintet"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["H, Masekela","H. Maekela","H. Masakela","H. Masekala","H. Masekeia","H. Masekela","H. Massekela","H. Msakela","H., Masekela","H.Masekala","H.Masekela","Huch Masekela","Hugh","Hugh Masakela","Hugh Masekala","Hugh Masekela & Company","Hugh Masekela's","Hugh Masekla","Hugh Maskella","Hugh Msekela","Hugh Ramopolo Masakela","Hugh Ramopolo Masekela","Hugh. Masekela","Masakela","Masekela","Masekela \"The Disco Kid\"","Masekele","Masequela","Maskela","The People","ヒュー・マサケラ","ヒュー・マセケラ"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/14661-Hugh-Masekela","type":"artist","urls":["http://hughmasekela.co.za/","https://www.facebook.com/HughMasekelaZA/","https://myspace.com/hughmasakela","https://twitter.com/hughmasekela","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_Masekela","https://dougpayne.com/hmhome.htm","https://www.allmusic.com/artist/hugh-masekela-mn0000830319","https://www.redbullmusicacademy.com/lectures/hugh-masekela-the-message","https://sahistory.org.za/people/hugh-masekela"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/147379/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"147379","image":"https://i.discogs.com/qGhpFcGn0vACrgJtthx97wVzfg-64pYFkcfXv7kMG-E/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:404/w:590/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE0NzM3/OS0xNTM4NTcxNTU0/LTQyNDUuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/ehlkG7NK6XcMcOu35caYmx9eAJqvulpoNOJqMS9lYxo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE0NzM3/OS0xNTM4NTcxNTU0/LTQyNDUuanBl